# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recon output — bulky, regenerable, and sometimes sensitive.
# The durable record of a target is scope.md + notes.md + findings/, all of
# which ARE tracked. Raw tool dumps are not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
recon/*/subdomains.txt
recon/*/urls.txt
recon/*/ports.txt
recon/*/live.txt
recon/*/*.json
recon/*/*.csv
recon/*/*.xml
recon/*/screenshots/
recon/*/scripts/

# Per-target PoC scripts. These are usually one-off curl/nmap invocations
# written to /tmp/work; anything worth keeping belongs in research/notes/ or
# docs/templates/ instead.
recon/*/poc/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Credentials and capture material — never commit, ever.
# If you save a session cookie or a bearer token, it goes in a local file
# that is gitignored. notes.md must never contain a live token.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.keystore
credentials*
*cookie*.txt
*session*.json
secrets/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kali scratch — per AGENTS.md, work happens in /tmp/work inside WSL and only
# finished files get copied back. Nothing here should ever land on D:.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/tmp/
work/
scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tooling / editor noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~